  m_Name: Orbicularis_oculi_muscle.L
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ModelPartDataSO
  id: Orbicularis_oculi_muscle.L
  partName: Orbicularis oculi muscle L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This circular muscle surrounds the eye and is responsible for closing the eyelids.
    It plays a crucial role in blinking, which helps keep the eyes moist and protected
    from debris. It is also involved in voluntary eye closure, such as squinting
    or tightly shutting the eyes. '
  - The muscle works continuously to maintain eye health by distributing tears evenly
    across the surface of the eye, preventing dryness and irritation while contributing
    to expressive facial movements.
